### 5. Competitor Audit & Differentiation
- **Supplied Competitor URL:** [https://www.caratlane.com/jewellery/red+stone+earrings.html](https://www.caratlane.com/jewellery/red+stone+earrings.html)
- **Competitor Structure:** Thin e-commerce listing page with basic product grids, gemstone filters (Ruby, Synthetic stones), and generic category descriptions (~350 words).
- **Competitor Omissions:** No deep gemological guidance on natural vs heat-treated gemstones, no explanation of BIS 6-digit alphanumeric HUID verification, no coverage of mandatory net weight billing rules, no prong setting durability analysis, and no fine jewellery maintenance protocols.
- **BlueStone Differentiation:** A comprehensive 4,982-word authority guide establishing consumer trust. Features Mohs hardness analysis across 4 red gemstones, gold alloy thermal/durability comparisons (18Kt vs 14Kt), legal net weight billing calculation walkthroughs, an interactive 3D Coverflow carousel with 6 authentic BlueStone 18Kt/14Kt designs, 3 custom Type 3 studio images, and 7 visible FAQs backed by schema.

---

### 6. Factual Grounding & Regulatory Citations
1. **BIS Hallmarking & HUID:** Bureau of Indian Standards (BIS) Hallmarking Regulations under IS 1417:2019 / BIS Act 2016. Verified mandatory 6-digit alphanumeric Hallmark Unique Identification Number (HUID) laser-engraved alongside the BIS triangular mark and purity stamp (750 for 18Kt, 585 for 14Kt). Verified verification steps via the official BIS CARE mobile application.
2. **Net Weight Billing Mandate:** Legal Metrology (Packaged Commodities) Rules & BIS Jeweller Code of Practice. Under Indian consumer protection regulations, jewellers must deduct all gemstone and enamel weight, billing gold metal strictly on net gold weight. Provided exact arithmetic formula for buyers.
3. **Goods and Services Tax (GST):** Standard 3% GST on fine gold jewellery and studded gemstones, plus 5% GST on making charges.
4. **Gemological Hardness & Care Standards:** GIA colored gemstone grading scales (Hue, Tone, Saturation) and Mohs mineral hardness benchmarks: Corundum/Ruby (Mohs 9), Pyrope/Almandine Garnet (Mohs 7–7.5), Rubellite Tourmaline (Mohs 7–7.5), and Organic Red Coral (Mohs 3.5). Explicit ultrasonic cleaning warnings provided for porous coral and fractured stones.

